    "case_id": "611",
    "case_summary": "A 22-year-old Japanese man (BMI: 22.7 kg/m²) with no medical history or family history developed fever and erythema on trunk and extremities 3 days after receiving first dose of Moderna vaccine. On the 12th day after second vaccination, he developed fever. Initial symptoms gradually worsened leading to hospitalization on the 24th day after second vaccination. After initial discharge, he was readmitted for chest pain.\n\nInitial presentation included fever and erythema on the trunk and extremities. During readmission, patient presented with chest pain that was refractory and persistent.\n\nLaboratory Tests (Initial admission):- C-reactive protein: 19.77 mg/dL (normal, <0.15 mg/dL)- Leukocyte count: 12,480/μL (normal, 3,500−9,700/μL)- Platelet count: 271 × 10³/μL (normal, 140−379 × 10³/μL)- Serum ferritin: 443.1 ng/mL (normal, 21−282 ng/mL)- D-dimer: 1.1 µg/mL (normal, <1.0 µg/mL)Laboratory Tests (Readmission):- High-sensitivity troponin I: 6327 pg/mL (normal, <26.2 pg/mL)- Creatine phosphokinase: 325 U/L (normal, 38−196 U/L)- D-dimer: 1.6 µg/mL- Platelet count: 87 × 10³/μLImaging Studies:1. Initial contrast-enhanced CT:- Revealed hepatosplenomegaly- Contrast-enhanced defective area in kidney2. Coronary angiography:- Total occlusion of atrioventricular branch of right coronary artery- 90% stenotic lesions with >3 mm coronary ectasia in left circumflex artery3. Optical coherence tomography:- Showed blurring of intravascular structure- Intimal thickening- Medial vessel destruction- Thrombi in RCA and LCx lesions4. Follow-up contrast-enhanced CT:- New intrahepatic arterial luminal irregularities- Enlarged contrast-enhanced defective area in kidneySARS-CoV-2 PCR test results were repeatedly negative",
